teens. On her head were the large ears characteristic of the dogpeople, and in her hand, she held what appeared to be a twig—and a
rather unimpressive one at that, considering it looked like something
she’d simply picked off the ground somewhere. Her young body was
slender, her pale skin covered with a minimum of clothing in a way
Page | 30
that seemed oddly provocative. Her short hair was silver, except for
one distinctive lock of her bangs where there was a shock of red.
